## Summary
KT SAT, with 32 years of experience in satellite management, is now tackling a new challenge in operating satellites in low Earth orbit, expanding beyond traditional geostationary satellite services.

## Key Points
- KT SAT has been managing satellites for over 32 years at an altitude of 36,000 km.
- The company is now focusing on low Earth orbit operation as a new strategic direction.
- This shift represents a technological challenge and potential advancement in satellite technology.
- The move may enhance satellite communication capabilities or reduce latency.
- The article highlights industry trends in satellite operations and emerging technologies.


